The Supplier will supply Supplier Personnel for these roles: {{supply.roles}}, at these Sites: {{supply.sites}}.

Each person supplied must:
- hold a valid SIA licence of the following category for the work they will do: {{supply.licence_categories}};
- have the competence, training and experience the Company asks for, including: {{supply.competence}};
- have been screened and vetted, and have had their right to work in the UK checked, as set out in this agreement;
- complete the Company's site induction before working their first shift at a Site.

Before anyone works their first shift, the Supplier will give the Company evidence of their identity, licence, right-to-work check, screening and training. The Company may also check any licence on the SIA's public register and carry out its own checks. The Company may refuse anyone for whom the evidence is missing or does not meet these requirements.

**The Supplier** is responsible for:
- employing or engaging Supplier Personnel and setting their terms;
- paying Supplier Personnel, including holiday pay, sick pay and any pension contributions, and deducting and paying tax and National Insurance contributions as the law requires;
- the licence, right-to-work and screening checks before supply, and keeping them up to date;
- the training and competence it has confirmed;
- dealing with Supplier Personnel's grievances and discipline as their employer or engager, with the Company's co-operation.

**The Company** is responsible for:
- directing and supervising Supplier Personnel's work at each Site;
- site induction, assignment instructions and Site-specific health and safety information;
- recording hours worked and approving timesheets;
- giving the Supplier the information it needs to meet its own legal duties, including those described in the agency workers clause.

This allocation does not change the duties each party keeps under the clause on legal duties.
